course: dictionary
lesson: 14437
title: Pairing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pairing is two people or things put together, like a pair or a team. «The teacher made a pairing of Sam and Priya for the task.» Here, pairing means putting two pupils together to work as a team.
explain: Pairing can also mean the act of putting things into pairs. «Pairing socks» means matching two socks that go together. Read the words around the word to find out which meaning fits.
explain: In technology, pairing means connecting two devices. «Bluetooth pairing» joins your headphones to your phone so they can work together. Ask yourself: are the things people, objects, or devices?
fact: Pairing can be a noun (a pairing, pairings) or the -ing form of the verb pair.
fact: A pairing is two people or things put together as a pair or team.
fact: «Pairing up» means joining with one partner to work together.
fact: «A good pairing» means two things that go well together, like cheese and apple.
fact: In maths, pairing numbers such as 1 and 9 helps you add quickly, because they make 10.
exercise: «The teacher made a pairing of Sam and Priya for the task.» What is a pairing here? | A loud noise | A kind of weather | A large bag | *Two people put together as a team
exercise: «Pairing socks» means matching two socks that go together. What does pairing mean in this phrase? | *Putting things into pairs | Throwing socks away | Losing one sock | Wearing socks in bed
exercise: Ben wants his headphones to play music from his phone. What does he need? | *Bluetooth pairing | A longer cable | A bigger screen | A new battery
test: «Cheese and apple is a good pairing.» What does a good pairing mean? | *Two things that go well together | Something very old | A type of sports shoe | Two things that clash badly
test: In maths, what is pairing 2 and 8 useful for? | Telling the time | *Adding quickly, because 2 + 8 = 10 | Measuring length | Drawing a picture
exam: Which sentence uses pairing as a verb? | «Our pairing won the match.» | *«She is pairing the socks by colour.» | «The pairing was in the car park.» | «A pairing is a pair of shoes.»
